    "body": "WATER AUTHORITY — FIELD NOTE — UNFILED\n\nThe underbridge settlements do not appear on any register, which is the point of them.\n\nThey catch rain off the roadbed above. The camber does the work; a length of gutter and a drum does the rest. It is not licensed and it is not clean and it is, I am obliged to record, extremely efficient. I counted forty-one people under the Sungai crossing alone.\n\nThey call themselves orang bawah. Under-people. They said it to me before I could say anything to them — the way you take a word first so it cannot be used on you later.\n\nA woman there asked whether I had come to take the drums. I said I had come to count. She said that was what the last one said.\n\nMy duty under the Statutes is to report unlicensed catchment.\n\nI have now written this note four times and filed none of them.",
